Patent Notice
====================================

There may be patents related to certain SCION technologies for which
an open-source patent pledge was issued.

Known pledges are listed below. Their terms and patents covered are available
at the respective link: 

- Anapaya Systems AG:
    https://learn.anapaya.net/docs/resources/patent-pledge/
    Last accessed: 9 September 2026
    The pledge applies to Free or Open Source Software and internal-only use,
    not to hardware or to distribution in combination with proprietary software.


Patent-Covered Contributions
============================

If you are contributing code that you know or believe implements a technique
covered by a patent, you are encouraged to follow the disclosure steps described
in https://docs.scion.org/en/latest/dev/contribute.html


FAQ
===


1. Can I use this implementation in spite of the patents?

  Yes. The core SCION protocol is free of patents.
  All components can be used according to the Apache 2.0 license,
  except components listed under question 2.

2. Which parts of the codebase implement a patented technique?

  Components of this repository that may leverage a patent pledge are:

  - scion/gateway (EP3756317B1, CN111771359B, US11240140B2)

  Search the codebase for the PATENT-NOTICE marker to find
  affected files.

3. Can I contribute a feature covered by a patent?

  If you know that your contribution is covered by patents, and you
  are not a patent owner, you must disclose it according to 
  https://docs.scion.org/en/latest/dev/contribute.html
  Use of your contribution use would be dependent on a patent pledge.

  If you are contributing code implementing one of your own patents,
  note that by contributing the code you grant patent licenses for this
  contribution under Apache-2.0 Section 3.

  At the time of writing (September 2026), only Anapaya Systems is known
  to hold patents on SCION, and their patents fall under the pledge
  linked above, which covers FOSS development, distribution,
  and internal-only use, but not distribution combined with proprietary
  software or hardware. The pledge itself is the ultimate source of truth;
  this is only a summary and does not modify or supersede it. 


  

4. I have more questions:

  Feel free to contact the SCION Association at info@scion.org 
